{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #876: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $A=\\{a_1<a_2<\\cdots\\}\\subset \\mathbb{N}$ be an infinite sum-free set - that is, there are no solutions to\\[a=b_1+\\cdots+b_r\\]with $b_1<\\cdots<b_r<a\\in A$. How small can $a_{n+1}-a_n$ be? Is it possible that $a_{n+1}-a_n<n$? Current best: Luczak and Schoen \\cite{LuSc00} have proved that, for all large $N$,\\[\\lvert A\\cap [1,N]\\rvert\\ll (N\\log N)^{1/2},\\]and that there exists a sum-free set $B$ such that\\[\\lvert B\\cap [1,N]\\rvert \\gg \\frac{N^{1/2}}{(\\log N)^{1/2+o(1)}}\\]for all large $N$. Prize: no. Tags: additive combinatorics."},"claim_id":"vcl_df1c0e1bc8867e0f8b7ad0805be0bab1161fea4d843ac438bc710683cb77780e","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:876","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_7a5d167299b01908","object_root":"sha256:0eff760f7da24ac18aa58d5542d52682a46fa9639c9a2100fd2e26fb46e244cd","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_re